 CROSS-CHECK

 Two independent product paths ran in the same session and agree exactly:

   AdbApplicationInventoryProvider.collect()   total 333 | third-party 4 | CYVRA 0
   HostVerificationProvider.verifyPostReset()  total 333 | third-party 4 | CYVRA 0

 The inventory figure (333 total, 4 third-party, 0 CYVRA) also matches the
 12-Oct-2026 factory-reset proof, which recorded 363 -> 333 total and
 40 -> 4 third-party. Source: docs/CYVRA_FACTORY_RESET_PROOF_2026-10-12.md
 section 3.1. The device therefore remains in its post-reset state and has
 not been re-populated since 12-Oct.

 WHAT THIS RUN DOES NOT ESTABLISH
 - It does not establish erasure. The screen-lock limitation above is
   unchanged and the product still reports PARTIALLY_VERIFIED, never VERIFIED.
 - It does not measure accounts, contacts or media. Those sources sit
   outside HostSecurityAuditEngine.ALLOWED_ADB_PREFIXES and are disclosed
   as not measured rather than implied by the three counts above.
 - userDataInaccessible stayed null (NOT ESTABLISHED) by design.
